schema: "0.4"
id: phosphor-01-query-and-answer
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns (a CLI learning tool) — Query & Answer, the /query terminal output. HERO screen.
# Theme tenets: monochrome amber CRT, single glowing hue on warm near-black, fixed-width mono as the primary UI face, radius 0, box-drawing chrome, zero elevation.
# Palette: amber #ffb000, warm near-black #140c00, dim amber #c88a00, bright amber #ffd050 (no error red on this screen).

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a
    monochrome amber-CRT terminal — ONE warm amber hue on a warm near-black void,
    fixed-width monospace as the primary UI face for everything (not a code accent),
    radius 0, box-drawing chrome, zero elevation. Terse, machine, all-business
    register — the UI reports, it does not chat or decorate. This is a real terminal
    window, never a web page.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a single amber-on-black TERMINAL WINDOW showing the
    calibrated answer output of a command-line learning tool (robot-learns). Fill the
    frame with ONE terminal window — a thin top title bar reads the working directory
    and shell; there is NO web browser chrome, no tabs, no address bar, no rounded
    website panels.

    Everything is a single warm AMBER hue on a warm near-black background — one glowing
    color only, with hierarchy carried by BRIGHTNESS (bright vs dim amber), never by
    other colors. Fixed-width monospaced type for absolutely everything: headings, body,
    labels, data.

    OVERALL LAYOUT (stacked terminal rows, top to bottom):

    TOP RULE: a horizontal box-drawing rule with a title notched into it reading
    "┤ robot-learns · query ├" at the left; at the right end of the same rule a small
    bracketed EXPERTISE BADGE "[ rust · advanced ]" in brighter amber.

    PROMPT LINE: a command line in bright amber — a ">" prompt glyph then the typed
    question "how does tokio park idle worker threads?" with a solid block cursor at
    the end of the line.

    CALIBRATED ANSWER BLOCK: 8–12 rows of dense monospaced answer text wrapping at
    roughly an 80-character measure, in mid amber, explaining the answer at an advanced
    level; one or two lines of technical/literal content are shown BRIGHTER and heavier
    (not a different color) to stand out, the way a mono terminal differentiates code by
    weight, not by a syntax rainbow.

    MACHINE / ENV PROFILE: a small box-drawn region titled "┤ ENV ├" holding three
    dim-amber key:value rows — "os : arch linux", "shell : zsh", "rust : 1.84 (rustup)".
    No background fill, just the box-drawing rule around it; the near-black void shows
    through.

    RELATED TOPICS: a row of bracketed mono chips in dim amber —
    "[ tokio::runtime ]  [ work-stealing ]  [ async parking ]".

    DEPTH INDICATOR: a single inline meter drawn with block characters showing verbosity
    level, e.g. "depth ▓▓▓▓░ advanced", in dim amber.

    BOTTOM STATUS RULE: a persistent reverse-video status bar (amber fill, near-black
    text) across the full width — keybind hints "^S save   ^R related   ^Q quit" at the
    left and a confirmation "✓ saved → kb/rust/tokio-scheduler.md" at the right.

    PALETTE & TYPE: strictly monochrome warm amber on warm near-black — a single glowing
    amber with dim and bright steps and nothing else; no green, no blue, no rainbow.
    Fixed-width terminal font throughout, no proportional or sans typeface anywhere.
    Crisp, high-contrast, slightly alive.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: zero rounded corners — every region is a sharp rectangle bounded by
    thin amber box-drawing rules at reduced intensity; no drop shadows, no gradients, no
    glow bloom, no scanlines, no screen curvature. Flat amber light on a dark void.

    MOOD: a warm vintage amber CRT terminal — one color, all business, focused and
    machine-calm; the feeling of a single amber lamp lighting a dark room.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, web browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, rounded website cards, syntax-highlighting rainbow, green terminal text, CRT scanlines, screen glow bloom, screen curvature"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Reads as a /query terminal session: prompt line + question, a dense calibrated answer block, an expertise badge, a box-drawn ENV profile, bracketed related-topic chips, a depth meter, and a bottom keybind status rule"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Monochrome amber on warm near-black, fixed-width mono for ALL text (no proportional face), radius 0, box-drawing rules not shadowed cards — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Clear terminal hierarchy by brightness; plausible real-CLI layout; grid-aligned rows"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts, no CRT filter kitsch"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "web browser chrome or a marketing web page instead of a terminal window"
    - "more than one hue (green/blue/rainbow) instead of monochrome amber"

tags: [phosphor, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup]
